17592186045443 true] [17592186672021 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 6 & 12\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nFirst reduce the matrix to row echelon form, making each pivot equal to $1$.\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=R_{2}+\\left(3\\right)R_{1}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 6 & 12\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_{3}:=R_{3}+\\left(-2\\right)R_{1}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_{2}\\leftrightarrow R_{3}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only.\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}+\\left(-2\\right)R_{2}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + 3 z &=-4 \\\\ y &=4 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe final equation is $0=0$, so it imposes no restriction. The basic variables are $x$ and $y$, and the free variable is $z$. Find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$. Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=- 3 z - 4 \\\\ y &=4 \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ is an arbitrary real number. In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}- 3 z - 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n" 13194139538686 17592186045443 true] [17592186672022 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}- 3 z - 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538686 17592186045443 true] [17592186672022 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13